course: dictionary
lesson: 5445
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one is meant. The word land is a good example. «Much of Earth's fresh water is frozen in ice sheets, huge sheets of ice covering land, and glaciers, slow rivers of ice.» Here land means the ground, the part of the Earth that is not water.
explain: «The same piece has three names: a meteoroid while it is in space, a meteor while it glows in the air, and a meteorite if any of it lands on the ground.» Here lands is a verb. To land means to come down to the ground or water after flying or falling. Check it by swapping in «comes down»: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «But this is not only history: about 476 million Indigenous people live today, and many are bringing back their languages, rights and lands.» Here lands means areas of ground that people own or use. The clue is the word rights: people fight for the right to their own land. Land can also mean a whole country, as in «a land far away».
fact: Land can be a noun (the ground, or a country) or a verb (to come down).
fact: «Land» means the part of the Earth that is not water.
fact: «Land» as a verb means to come down onto the ground or water after flying or falling.
fact: «On land» means on the ground, not in water, and «dry land» means ground that is not covered by water.
fact: The plural «lands» can mean areas of ground that someone owns or uses, like farms.
exercise: «Much of Earth's fresh water is frozen in ice sheets, huge sheets of ice covering land.» What does land mean here? | A coin landing on heads | A flight ending at the airport | A boat brought to the shore | * The ground, the part of Earth that is not water
exercise: «...a meteorite if any of it lands on the ground.» What does lands mean here? | Glows brightly in the air | * Comes down to the ground | Owns a farm | Floats in space
exercise: In «The plane will land at noon», what kind of word is land? | * A verb, an action word | A noun, a naming word | An adjective, a describing word | A plural, more than one
test: «You smell cookies baking from the other room because tiny invisible bits of the cookies have floated through the air, up your nose, and landed on smell cells.» What does landed mean here? | Ran away from | Cooked slowly | * Came to rest on | Sang loudly
test: In «a land far away», what does land mean? | A boat brought to the shore | Ground that someone farms | * A country or place | Coming down from the sky
exam: «Pollen from the feathery tassel on top must land on that silk or the kernel never grows.» Which word could replace land here? | Dance across | Hide under | * Come down onto | Rise up from
